<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's Engro rises 4.53 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's Engro rises 4.53 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engro Chemical Pakistan Ltd's 10-rupee stock rose 8.50 rupees, or 4.53 percent, to 196 on Wednesday after its annual profits jumped, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 14,200 shares of the blue chip had changed hands by noon at the Karachi Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Engro, Pakistan's second largest urea manufacturer with a market share of almost 24 percent, last week announced an 80 percent cash dividend for calendar 1996, compared to 60 percent the previous year. It also gave 25 percent bonus stocks for 1996, compared to 20 percent for 1995.</p>
<p>Net profit rose to 1.386 billion rupees from 782 million.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
